# The .eh_frame issue is complex. For now, let me just emit the EXACT same .eh_frame
# as TCC does by replicating the byte sequence.
# 
# The reference .eh_frame for a simple function (from test_min.o):
# CIE (24 bytes total):
# 14 00 00 00  = length 20
# 00 00 00 00  = CIE ID
# 01           = version
# 7a 52 00     = "zR" augmentation
# 01           = code align factor
# 78           = data align factor (-8)
# 10           = return addr reg (RIP)
# 01           = aug data len
# 1b           = aug data (pcrel+sdata4)
# 0c 07 08     = DW_CFA_def_cfa RSP+8
# 90 01        = DW_CFA_offset r16 @cfa-8
# 00 00 00     = pad to 4 bytes
#
# FDE (36 bytes total):
# 20 00 00 00  = length 32
# 1c 00 00 00  = CIE offset (== offset of CIE pointer field from section start)
# 00 00 00 00  = PC begin (relocated: .text + 0)
# 12 00 00 00  = PC range (size of function = 0x12)
# 00           = aug len
# 41           = DW_CFA_advance_loc 1 (push rbp takes 1 byte)
# 0e 10        = DW_CFA_def_cfa_offset 16
# 86 02        = DW_CFA_offset r6 (rbp) at cfa-16
# 43           = DW_CFA_advance_loc 3 (mov rbp,rsp takes 3 bytes)
# 0d 06        = DW_CFA_def_cfa_register r6 (rbp)
# 04 0d 00 00 00 = DW_CFA_advance_loc4 13 (rest of function after frame setup)
# 0c 07 08     = DW_CFA_def_cfa RSP+8 (epilogue)
# 00 00 00     = padding

# My implementation generates something similar but with wrong relocations.
# Let me rewrite emit_eh_frame to match TCC's output exactly.

